  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14176224/assets/1fab2b2158183c89fb48259408e3a1c684af657cd34d68d4b79e4773a4251f37.png)\n\nIn the figure shown above, determine the measure of $∠GOH$ given that $m∠BOD={120}^{∘}.$",
  "worked_solution": "From the diagram, $∠AOC$ and $∠EOG$ are vertical angles. Since vertical angles are congruent, we have\n\n$$\nm∠AOC=m∠EOG={90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, since $∠AOC$ is a right angle, the angle addition postulate gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB+m∠BOC & =m∠AOC \\\\ {30}^{∘}+m∠BOC & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠BOC & ={60}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, given that $m∠BOD={120}^{∘}$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOC+m∠COD & =m∠BOD \\\\ {60}^{∘}+m∠COD & ={120}^{∘} \\\\ m∠COD & ={60}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $∠COD$ and $∠GOH$ are vertical angles. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm∠GOH=m∠COD={60}^{∘}.\n$$",
